+# Spec 2: Splitting a damage charge loses a cent
+
+## Outcome
+
+When a damage charge does not divide evenly between its borrowers, every cent is still billed to someone.
+Charge D-301 (£33.33, two borrowers) gives £16.67 and £16.66, and the shares add up to £33.33.
+
+## Requirements
+
+- The system shall make the shares returned by `splitCharge` add up to exactly the charge, in integer cents.
+- When the charge does not divide evenly, the system shall give each borrower either the rounded-down share or one cent more.
+- When the charge does not divide evenly, the system shall give the leftover cents one each to the first borrowers in the list, so the result is the same every time.
+- When the charge divides evenly, the system shall give every borrower the same share.
+- The system shall make `bun run desk split <charge-id>` report shares that add up to the charge.
+- If the charge is not a whole number of cents or is negative, or the number of borrowers is not a whole number of at least 1, the system shall refuse the split with an error.
+
+## Must not change
+
+- Amounts stay integer cents; no floats are used for an amount.
+- Even splits and single-borrower splits give the same results as today.
+- A negative charge is still refused.
+- `src/auth/` is not touched.
+- The `desk split` output format stays the same: one `<member>  £<amount>` line per borrower, then the summary line.
+
+## Out of scope
+
+- Weighted or unequal splits chosen by the desk.
+- Changing the stored damage charges or the seed data.
+- Late fees and any other command.
+
+## Done when
+
+- The new tests in `tests/fees/split.test.ts` pass, and the existing tests still pass.
+- `bun run gate` exits 0.
diff --git a/tests/fees/split.test.ts b/tests/fees/split.test.ts
index 936c6bf..7f1588d 100644
--- a/tests/fees/split.test.ts
+++ b/tests/fees/split.test.ts
@@ -12,3 +12,53 @@ test("one borrower pays the whole charge", () => {
 test("a negative charge is refused", () => {
   expect(() => splitCharge(-1, 2)).toThrow();
 });
+
+const sum = (xs: number[]) => xs.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0);
+
+test("the shares add up to the charge", () => {
+  expect(sum(splitCharge(3333, 2))).toBe(3333);
+  for (let total = 0; total <= 200; total++) {
+    for (let ways = 1; ways <= 7; ways++) {
+      expect(sum(splitCharge(total, ways))).toBe(total);
+    }
+  }
+});
+
+test("an uneven charge gives each borrower the rounded-down share or one cent more", () => {
+  for (let total = 0; total <= 200; total++) {
+    for (let ways = 1; ways <= 7; ways++) {
+      const shares = splitCharge(total, ways);
+      expect(shares.length).toBe(ways);
+      expect(sum(shares)).toBe(total);
+      const floor = Math.floor(total / ways);
+      for (const s of shares) {
+        expect(Number.isInteger(s)).toBe(true);
+        expect(s === floor || s === floor + 1).toBe(true);
+      }
+    }
+  }
+});
+
+test("leftover cents go one each to the first borrowers", () => {
+  expect(splitCharge(3333, 2)).toEqual([1667, 1666]);
+  expect(splitCharge(100, 3)).toEqual([34, 33, 33]);
+  expect(splitCharge(101, 3)).toEqual([34, 34, 33]);
+  expect(splitCharge(2, 5)).toEqual([1, 1, 0, 0, 0]);
+});
+
+test("an even charge gives every borrower the same share", () => {
+  expect(splitCharge(900, 3)).toEqual([300, 300, 300]);
+  expect(splitCharge(0, 4)).toEqual([0, 0, 0, 0]);
+});
+
+test("desk split reports shares that add up to the charge", () => {
+  const run = Bun.spawnSync(["bun", "run", "src/desk.ts", "split", "D-301"], { cwd: `${import.meta.dir}/../..` });
+  const out = run.stdout.toString();
+  expect(out).toContain("shares add up to £33.33");
+});
+
+test("a bad charge or borrower count is refused", () => {
+  expect(() => splitCharge(10.5, 2)).toThrow();
+  expect(() => splitCharge(100, 0)).toThrow();
+  expect(() => splitCharge(100, 1.5)).toThrow();
+});
